// Extracted from Type Siege when a second word game became likely (Word Hunt, a daily guesser,
// anagrams…): every consumer gets the same vocabulary AND, more importantly, the same MATCHING
// rules. Two games rolling their own diacritic folding would disagree in edge cases and each
// would be subtly wrong in a different language.
//
//   window.KOMYO_WORDS.banks[<locale>]        → array of words (lower-case, letters only)
//   window.KOMYO_WORDS.fold(s)                → diacritic-insensitive key ('żółw' → 'zolw')
//   window.KOMYO_WORDS.translit(s)            → Ukrainian Cyrillic → Latin ('жаба' → 'zhaba')
//   window.KOMYO_WORDS.bands(locale)          → { short:[], medium:[], long:[] } rank THIRDS of
//                                               that locale's own length-sorted list, so absolute
//                                               letter counts can't make Polish permanently harder
//   window.KOMYO_WORDS.byLength(locale,min,max)
//
// Bank sizes differ by locale and always will — nothing may assume they match.
